From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 04/18] feat: Solar Hijri (Jalali) calendar for displayed dates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

VERSION: 3.1 (2026-10-15)  3.1 = Gregorian month header like the Jalali one
  (month centered, previous/next buttons on both sides, pointing outwards).
  Before: 3.0 (2026-10-15)  3.0 = + Gregorian | Jalali switch inside the calendar (old 0019).
  Before: 2.0 (2026-10-12)  2.0 = merged set of 11 patches (old numbers below)
Root: build/outline-1.11.0 (apply after 0001..0003)

(was 0007 v1.0)
- New user preferences: Calendar (gregorian | persian), defaulting to
  Persian when the interface language is Persian, and Date format (month
  names | numeric yyyy/MM/dd) for the Persian calendar. Both are validated
  by the API and shown in Settings > Preferences.
- formatDate() in shared/utils/date wraps date-fns format: in the Persian
  calendar the year, month and day tokens are converted with Intl (no new
  dependency), day-month-year order for Persian, Persian digits; Intl
  formatters are cached.
- Used for timestamps, date mentions, history labels, expiry dates and the
  insert-date commands. Stored values stay Gregorian ISO strings.
- Date pickers show a Persian month grid (week starting Saturday) when the
  calendar is Persian; fromPersianDate() is the inverse of toPersianDate().

Switch inside the calendar (was 0019 v1.0):
The calendar opened from a date in a document has a small switch above the
month: Gregorian | Jalali (میلادی | شمسی). Choosing one changes the whole
calendar (month grid, month names, week start) and the date text shown in the
document. The choice is saved as the user's Calendar preference (the same one
as Settings > Preferences), so it stays the same after reload. Stored dates are
unchanged (Gregorian ISO).

The switch is shown only where a caller passes onCalendarChange (the date
mention picker); the API key expiry picker is unchanged.

